Why: Linux launches hand the front back only when the launched app (or a window new since the launch) took it, never a window the user switched to during the wait; a hotkey keeps every modifier when it looks for a menu shortcut (an unknown one matches no item), and a hotkey with only one of x or y is refused before the menu-shortcut route.

